  "id": "Compound::DB00296 - Gene::6335",
  "verbalization": "Ropivacaine, a local anesthetic, is linked to Scn9a through a shared pathway involving amides and anesthetic agents. The evidence suggests that Ropivacaine, as part of the amide class, binds to Scn9a, which is a key ion channel involved in pain transmission. This relationship is supported by multiple paths, all of which converge on the mechanism of action through the amide class and its interaction with Scn9a. The lowest common ancestors across the paths—such as Piperidinecarboxamide and Anesthetic Agent—highlight a common functional category, reinforcing the connection between Ropivacaine and Scn9a. The integration of these pathways underscores a consistent mechanism where amide-based anesthetics interact with Scn9a, contributing to the analgesic effects observed in clinical settings.",
